WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.960
The placement of a wireless access point in&nbsp;
a home or business network is crucial to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.320
speeds devices accessing the wireless&nbsp;
access point will be able to obtain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.960
First, wireless access points should be&nbsp;
positioned in a room centrally, if possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.120
and above the ground so that the wireless&nbsp;
signal can travel as clearly as possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.040
Secondly, avoid placing wireless access&nbsp;
points near items that can interfere with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.960
the wireless access point's signal. These&nbsp;
include microwave ovens, elevator shafts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.120
and water tanks, as these tend to be the&nbsp;
largest cause of signal interference.

